{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, Mr. Johnson. I’m Dr. Patel, one of the vascular surgery team. You’ve been admitted because of a narrowing in the stent that was placed in the artery to your transplanted kidney."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, right. I remember now. My blood pressure’s been high lately. Is that why?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Your ultrasound showed very high blood flow speeds in that artery—433 and 464 cm/sec—which suggests the stent is narrowing again. That’s called in-stent restenosis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So, will I need another procedure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:06:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Tomorrow, you’ll have an angiogram to look at the artery with imaging, and we’ll likely do an angioplasty to reopen the narrowed stent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:07:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it safe? I had the stent placed about a year ago."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a common follow-up. We use CO2 contrast, which is safer for your kidney function. You’ll also get extra fluids and medication to protect your kidneys."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:10:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. What about my other meds? Like my diabetes and transplant pills?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:11:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll keep taking all your regular medications, including tacrolimus and insulin. The transplant team checked your levels today—everything’s stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve been worried about my kidney."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:14:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re monitoring closely. Your creatinine is 1.8 today—slightly elevated but stable. That’s expected with the stent issue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:15:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the procedure—will I be asleep?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:16:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll be under light sedation. It’s not open surgery—just a small puncture in the groin to thread the catheter up to the kidney artery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And how long will I be here?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2193-07-10 20:19:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Likely two days. We’ll watch you closely after the procedure, especially your blood pressure and kidney function."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2193-07-11 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We’re getting ready for your procedure today. Any questions before we go over consent?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2193-07-11 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No new questions. Just want to make sure the stent stays open this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2193-07-11 08:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll use a balloon to reopen it. Since it’s a repeat narrowing, we won’t place another stent—just open the existing one."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2193-07-11 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And I’ll be on blood thinners after?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2193-07-11 08:06:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. You’ll continue Plavix and aspirin to keep the stent open. No changes there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2193-07-11 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, Mr. Johnson. You’re back from the procedure. Everything went smoothly. We opened the narrowed stent, and blood flow is much better now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2193-07-11 13:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. Did you see why it narrowed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2193-07-11 13:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s common with stents, especially with underlying conditions like diabetes and high cholesterol. We’ll keep managing those to prevent it from happening again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2193-07-11 13:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My blood pressure was high before—should it come down now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2193-07-11 13:37:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we expect it to improve. We’ll keep monitoring it. You’re on lisinopril and amlodipine, which help, and we’ll continue those."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2193-07-11 13:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my kidney—will this help it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2193-07-11 13:40:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Better blood flow means better function. Your creatinine was 1.8 this morning—same as before—so no damage, but we’ll check again tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2193-07-11 13:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve been tired lately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2193-07-11 13:43:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s common with high blood pressure and kidney issues. You should start feeling better as things stabilize."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2193-07-11 19:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow morning. You’ve been stable all day, and your labs look good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2193-07-11 19:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2193-07-11 19:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep the groin site clean and dry. You can shower, but no heavy lifting—nothing over five pounds—for at least a week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2193-07-11 19:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What if I see bleeding?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2193-07-11 19:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If there’s sudden swelling or bleeding, lie down, keep your leg straight, and press firmly on the site. If it doesn’t stop, go to the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2193-07-11 19:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2193-07-11 19:10:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All the same. Aspirin, Plavix, your blood pressure meds, insulin, and transplant drugs. No changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2193-07-11 19:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "When do I follow up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2193-07-11 19:13:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Vascular surgery in two weeks for an ultrasound. Transplant nephrology will also see you soon to keep monitoring your kidney."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2193-07-11 19:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks, Doctor. I feel much better knowing we caught this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2193-07-11 19:16:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did well. Rest tonight, and we’ll get you home tomorrow. Call us if you have fever, leg pain, or any issues with the incision."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2193-07-12 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. Final check before discharge. Blood pressure is 138/76, creatinine still stable. You’re good to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2193-07-12 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. I’ll take it easy and follow the instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2193-07-12 09:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Someone will bring your discharge papers and prescriptions. Drive safe when you’re off pain meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2193-07-12 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thanks for taking care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2193-07-12 09:06:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2193-07-10 19:42:00",
    "admission_end": "2193-07-12 13:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 60-year-old male with a history of kidney transplantation, type 2 diabetes, hypertension, and hyperlipidemia was admitted for in-stent restenosis of the right transplanted renal artery, presenting with elevated blood pressure. A transplant kidney ultrasound revealed significantly increased renal artery velocities, confirming restenosis. The patient underwent an elective angioplasty of the existing renal artery stent via endovascular approach using CO2 contrast, with no complications. He remained hemodynamically stable throughout, with preserved renal function post-procedure. Pain was controlled, and he tolerated advancement of diet and activity. He was discharged home on dual antiplatelet therapy, antihypertensives, immunosuppressants, and insulin, with instructions for wound care, activity restrictions, and follow-up with vascular surgery and transplant nephrology.",
    "problems": [
      "Other complications due to genitourinary device, implant, and graft",
      "Kidney replaced by transplant",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Pure hypercholesterolemia",
      "Atherosclerosis of renal artery",
      "Hyperplasia of prostate, unspecified, without urinary obstruction and other lower urinary symptoms (LUTS)",
      "Surgical operation with implant of artificial internal device causing abnormal patient reaction, or later complication,without mention of misadventure at time of operation",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of other urinary organs",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin"
    ]
  }
}
